There is a single SKU with two ordering-code spellings, one technical table (transmit max 1360 nm and receiver range max 1600 nm), and protocol support **FE** and **STM1/OC3** on the same row. Modes below assign each pool value where the datasheet ties it (model variants, tx vs rx wavelength rows, product vs protocol standards).

```json
{
  "modes": [
    {
      "label": "SO-SFP-100BASE-EXD 100Base-EXD (TX)",
      "model": "SO-SFP-100BASE-EXD",
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1360.0,
      "standards_code": "100Base-EXD"
    },
    {
      "label": "SO-SFP-100Base-EXD 100Base-EXD (RX)",
      "model": "SO-SFP-100Base-EXD",
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1600.0,
      "standards_code": "100Base-EXD"
    },
    {
      "label": "FE",
      "model": "SO-SFP-100BASE-EXD",
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1600.0,
      "standards_code": "FE"
    },
    {
      "label": "STM1/OC3",
      "model": "SO-SFP-100BASE-EXD",
      "wavelength_max_nm": 1600.0,
      "standards_code": "STM1/OC3"
    }
  ]
}
```
